1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,348
Part 1. You will hear a
man phoning a holiday

2
00:00:03,372 --> 00:00:06,392
company to book a
canal narrowboat holiday.

3
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:10,940
First, you have some time
to look at questions 1 to 5.

4
00:00:12,210 --> 00:00:15,820
Now listen carefully and
answer questions 1 to 5.

5
00:00:46,219 --> 00:00:52,220
Good morning, Hartwell Waterways.
Lorna speaking. How can I help?

6
00:00:52,419 --> 00:00:56,640
Oh, hello. I'm hoping to book a
narrowboat for a week this summer.

7
00:00:57,495 --> 00:01:01,800
I've never done anything like
this before, so bear with me.

8
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:05,191
Not at all. Most of our
customers are first-timers.

9
00:01:05,215 --> 00:01:09,012
Let me just take a few details
first. Could I have your name?

10
00:01:09,339 --> 00:01:11,420
Yes, it's Martin Wardrop.

11
00:01:11,659 --> 00:01:17,320
Is that spelt like the furniture?
W-A-R-D-R-O-B-E?

12
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:26,380
Everybody says that. No, it's
W-A-R-D-R-O-P. There's no E on the end.

13
00:01:26,644 --> 00:01:30,780
W-A-R-D-R-O-P.

14
00:01:31,409 --> 00:01:34,280
Lovely.
And how many of you will be on the boat?

15
00:01:35,159 --> 00:01:38,497
Well, it was going to be six.
My sister and her husband

16
00:01:38,521 --> 00:01:41,992
were coming, but they've
had to pull out because of work.

17
00:01:42,449 --> 00:01:45,600
So it's just me, my wife
and our two boys now.

18
00:01:45,959 --> 00:01:48,220
So that's four of you all together then?

19
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:49,175
That's right.

20
00:01:49,199 --> 00:01:52,107
And how old are the
boys? We put life jackets on

21
00:01:52,131 --> 00:01:55,112
board, so I need to know
which sizes to give you.

22
00:01:55,400 --> 00:02:01,240
Nine and twelve. Well, the younger
one's nine now, but he'll be ten by August.

23
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:05,115
Two junior sizes then. And
they'll need to wear them on deck

24
00:02:05,139 --> 00:02:08,491
at all times, I'm afraid, even
if they're strong swimmers.

25
00:02:09,010 --> 00:02:11,380
They won't like that, but fair enough.

26
00:02:11,684 --> 00:02:16,200
And when were you thinking of going?
Our higher weeks run Saturday to Saturday.

27
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:22,970
Sometime in August. We'd set
off on Saturday the 23rd, I think.

28
00:02:22,994 --> 00:02:27,412
No, hang on, that's the day we'd have
to be home. So we'd set off on the 16th.

29
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:34,835
Departing the 16th of August, back on the
23rd. Yes, I've got boats available that week.

30
00:02:34,859 --> 00:02:38,692
Now, which of our bases would suit you?
There are three on this stretch of the canal.

31
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:42,480
The website mentions Stoke Lock.
That's the nearest one to us.

32
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:49,564
I'm afraid Stoke Lock is fully booked for the
whole of August. And Abbey Basin isn't really an

33
00:02:49,588 --> 00:02:53,672
option either, because the canals closed there
until September while they replaced the lock gates.

34
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:58,540
But we do have boats at Orchard Wharf,
which is only about 20 minutes further on.

35
00:02:58,785 --> 00:03:01,740
Orchard Wharf? That's fine.
We're driving anyway.

36
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:04,898
Speaking of which,
you can leave your car at

37
00:03:04,922 --> 00:03:07,652
the wharf while you're
away. It's £12 a day.

38
00:03:07,975 --> 00:03:12,860
£12 a day?
So that'd be, er, £84 for the week?

39
00:03:15,145 --> 00:03:19,267
No, no. If you pay for the whole
week up front, it's a flat rate of £45.

40
00:03:19,291 --> 00:03:23,032
It used to be free, but the
landowner started charging last year.

41
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:25,600
£45? That's not bad at all.

42
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:30,293
Er, one other thing that worries
me. Do we need any experience?

43
00:03:30,317 --> 00:03:33,332
I've only ever rode a
dinghy on a boating lake.

44
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:38,220
You'd be surprised how many
people say that. No experience needed.

45
00:03:39,070 --> 00:03:42,168
Before you leave, one of our
staff spends about an hour on the

46
00:03:42,192 --> 00:03:45,152
boat with you, showing you
how to steer and work the locks.

47
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:48,460
Right, shall I tell you about the
boats that are free that week?

48
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:49,660
Yes, please.

49
00:03:49,970 --> 00:03:52,614
Before you hear the
rest of the conversation,

50
00:03:52,638 --> 00:03:55,472
you have some time to
look at questions 6 to 10.

51
00:03:57,610 --> 00:04:00,680
Now listen and answer questions 6 to 10.

52
00:04:33,790 --> 00:04:37,798
OK, there are three. The first is Kingfisher.
She sleeps four, and she's the shortest of

53
00:04:37,822 --> 00:04:41,752
the three, which makes her much easier to
handle. We often recommend her to beginners.

54
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,860
That sounds ideal, actually.

55
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:52,847
The one thing people do comment on is the space.
The bedroom's fine, it's got a proper double bed,

56
00:04:52,871 --> 00:04:56,892
and the kitchen's very well equipped. But the shower
is really tiny. If you're tall, you'll notice.

57
00:04:57,350 --> 00:05:01,880
I'm six foot two, so noted.
And what does she cost?

58
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:09,820
In June, she'd be 980 pounds. But August is
peak season, so for your week, it's 1,160.

59
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:14,020
1,160. OK.

60
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:28,094
The second is Moorhen, which sleeps six, so you'd all have more room to
spread out. We used to provide a couple of kayaks with her, but there were

61
00:05:28,118 --> 00:05:32,346
rather too many, uh, accidents. So these days she comes with two bicycles
instead. They're handy for riding along the towpath to the village shops.

62
00:05:32,370 --> 00:05:35,560
Oh, the boys would love that.
Is there a catch?

63
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:43,934
She's one of our older boats. I wouldn't say the
engine's unreliable, because it was fully serviced

64
00:05:43,958 --> 00:05:47,812
in the spring, but it is quite loud, so whoever's
steering at the back will hear it all day.

65
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:50,840
Fair enough. And the price for Moorhen?

66
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:53,980
1,325 for the week.

67
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,240
Right.

68
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:04,780
And the third is Heron, our newest boat. She was only
launched in March, and she also sleeps six. People tend to

69
00:06:04,804 --> 00:06:09,226
assume she's got a washing machine, which she hasn't, but
she does have a dishwasher, and that always goes down well.

70
00:06:09,250 --> 00:06:12,200
My wife would be thrilled.
What's the downside?

71
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:19,641
She's the longest boat in the fleet, so she
can't turn round in some of the narrower

72
00:06:19,665 --> 00:06:23,492
sections, and you'd have to plan your
route much more carefully. She's 1,490.

73
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:28,450
Hmm. I was leaning towards
Kingfisher, but with my height,

74
00:06:28,474 --> 00:06:32,332
I think it'll be Moorhen.
The bike's swing it, really.

75
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:36,928
Lovely. I'll reserve her for you now.
We'll need a deposit of a quarter of

76
00:06:36,952 --> 00:06:41,032
the total within seven days, and I'll
email you the paperwork this afternoon.

77
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:44,440
Brilliant. Can I pay the
deposit by card over the phone?

78
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:48,654
You can, or by bank transfer if
you prefer. The details are on the

79
00:06:48,678 --> 00:06:52,852
confirmation email. The balance is
then due six weeks before you travel.

80
00:06:53,185 --> 00:06:56,700
Card's easiest.
Thanks so much for your help, Lorna.

81
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:59,304
That is the end of part one.

82
00:06:59,328 --> 00:07:03,692
You now have one minute to
check your answers to part one.

83
00:07:52,190 --> 00:07:53,240
Thank you.

84
