102
00:08:51,859 --> 00:08:55,260
Right, good evening everyone
and welcome to the Corrin Theatre.

103
00:08:55,459 --> 00:08:56,260
I'm Diane.

104
00:08:56,261 --> 00:08:58,850
I run front of house, which
means that for the next

105
00:08:58,874 --> 00:09:01,267
few months you'll be
seeing rather a lot of me.

106
00:09:01,268 --> 00:09:03,260
Thank you all for volunteering.

107
00:09:03,261 --> 00:09:06,248
We'll start with a quick tour
of the ground floor because

108
00:09:06,272 --> 00:09:09,272
the first thing audiences do
is ask you where things are.

109
00:09:09,709 --> 00:09:13,260
So, we're standing just inside the
main entrance, facing into the building.

110
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:16,126
The box office is right
here on your right, and

111
00:09:16,150 --> 00:09:19,272
the bar runs along the
whole of the left-hand wall.

112
00:09:19,709 --> 00:09:21,260
Now, the cloakroom.

113
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:23,273
Regular visitors will
tell you it's next to the

114
00:09:23,297 --> 00:09:25,272
box office, because
that's where it used to be.

115
00:09:25,459 --> 00:09:26,260
It isn't anymore.

116
00:09:26,261 --> 00:09:30,260
That space is now the shop,
selling programs and souvenirs.

117
00:09:30,859 --> 00:09:34,547
The cloakroom has moved to the
opposite side, in the corner immediately

118
00:09:34,571 --> 00:09:38,267
to your left as you come through
the doors, just before the bar begins.

119
00:09:38,268 --> 00:09:42,272
Straight ahead of us is the grand
staircase, which takes you up to the circle.

120
00:09:42,310 --> 00:09:46,260
And on either side of it, there's a
set of double doors into the stalls.

121
00:09:46,261 --> 00:09:49,317
To the left of the staircase, a
corridor runs all the way along the

122
00:09:49,341 --> 00:09:52,272
side of the auditorium, and
there's a matching one on the right.

123
00:09:52,909 --> 00:09:55,260
Let's take the left-hand corridor first.

124
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:59,260
The first door you come to,
on your left, says Technical Store.

125
00:09:59,261 --> 00:10:00,260
That's not ours.

126
00:10:00,261 --> 00:10:01,260
Please don't go in there.

127
00:10:01,261 --> 00:10:06,260
Keep walking right to the far end, and
the door facing you is the Volunteers Room.

128
00:10:06,559 --> 00:10:10,260
That's where you'll leave your bags, sign
in, and get your briefing before each show.

129
00:10:10,261 --> 00:10:13,260
People are always surprised
by where we've put the lift.

130
00:10:13,859 --> 00:10:16,260
You'd expect it beside the
main staircase, wouldn't you?

131
00:10:16,261 --> 00:10:17,261
But it isn't.

132
00:10:17,459 --> 00:10:19,775
It's tucked away in the
alcove at the far end of

133
00:10:19,799 --> 00:10:22,267
the bar, in the back
left-hand corner of the foyer.

134
00:10:22,268 --> 00:10:27,260
So if someone in a wheelchair asks, send
them past the bar, not towards the stairs.

135
00:10:27,261 --> 00:10:29,260
Now the right-hand corridor.

136
00:10:29,859 --> 00:10:32,260
About halfway along, on
your right, is the first aid room.

137
00:10:32,261 --> 00:10:36,260
Don't confuse it with the door
at the very end of that corridor.

138
00:10:36,509 --> 00:10:41,260
That leads backstage to the stage
door, and it's strictly for cast and crew.

139
00:10:41,359 --> 00:10:43,260
And finally, something
we're rather proud of.

140
00:10:43,261 --> 00:10:45,964
The little room underneath
the grand staircase, which you

141
00:10:46,002 --> 00:10:49,260
get into from the foyer,
used to be a storage cupboard.

142
00:10:49,261 --> 00:10:53,260
We've turned it into a quiet
room, for anyone, child or adult,

143
00:10:53,709 --> 00:10:57,260
who finds a performance overwhelming
and needs a few minutes somewhere calm.

144
00:10:57,809 --> 00:11:00,396
Before you hear the
rest of the talk, you

145
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:03,272
have some time to look
at questions 16 to 20.

146
00:11:33,709 --> 00:11:38,260
Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20.

147
00:11:38,261 --> 00:11:40,260
Right, a few things about the job itself.

148
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:43,260
First, what you wear.

149
00:11:43,509 --> 00:11:47,260
We'll issue each of you with a
burgundy waistcoat and a name badge.

150
00:11:47,559 --> 00:11:52,260
We used to hand out jackets, but under
the stage lights they were far too hot.

151
00:11:52,509 --> 00:11:55,260
What you wear underneath
is up to you, within reason.

152
00:11:56,009 --> 00:11:59,260
A plain white shirt and
dark trousers or a skirt.

153
00:11:59,759 --> 00:12:04,260
Some of you may have
heard that shirts must be black.

154
00:12:04,409 --> 00:12:07,260
That was the old rule, and it's gone.

155
00:12:07,261 --> 00:12:08,261
Shoes, though.

156
00:12:08,609 --> 00:12:13,260
I know you're on your feet for three hours,
but trainers aren't acceptable, I'm afraid.

157
00:12:13,459 --> 00:12:16,260
They need to be black and polished.

158
00:12:16,261 --> 00:12:17,261
Latecomers.

159
00:12:18,309 --> 00:12:21,264
In the past, we'd simply take
them in with a torch during

160
00:12:21,364 --> 00:12:25,260
the first scene, and it caused
absolute chaos in the rows.

161
00:12:25,261 --> 00:12:26,261
So that's stopped.

162
00:12:26,759 --> 00:12:29,105
Now they wait until the
stage manager radios

163
00:12:29,129 --> 00:12:31,267
through to say
there's a suitable break.

164
00:12:31,268 --> 00:12:34,260
And until then, they can follow
the show on the monitor in the foyer.

165
00:12:34,984 --> 00:12:39,260
And whatever you do, don't tell a
latecomer they'll get their money back.

166
00:12:39,310 --> 00:12:41,260
Refunds aren't your decision.

167
00:12:41,310 --> 00:12:43,260
That's entirely up to the box office.

168
00:12:44,659 --> 00:12:46,260
The interval.

169
00:12:46,310 --> 00:12:48,270
People think the interval
is all about ice creams.

170
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:52,260
And yes, some of you
will have a tray to sell from.

171
00:12:52,509 --> 00:12:54,745
But what I really need
is for you to stay in

172
00:12:54,769 --> 00:12:57,272
your section and keep
the aisles and exits clear,

173
00:12:57,809 --> 00:13:01,260
because that's when bags and coats
start piling up and someone trips.

174
00:13:02,259 --> 00:13:04,260
We did ask ushers to count
the audience at one time,

175
00:13:04,261 --> 00:13:07,260
but that's done electronically
from the tickets now.

176
00:13:07,261 --> 00:13:09,260
Fire procedures.

177
00:13:09,261 --> 00:13:12,260
Our alarm has two stages.

178
00:13:12,261 --> 00:13:15,260
The first is an intermittent tone.

179
00:13:15,261 --> 00:13:17,260
And that's an alert only.

180
00:13:17,809 --> 00:13:21,260
You don't move anyone and you
don't say a word to the audience.

181
00:13:21,859 --> 00:13:25,260
You go straight to the exit you've been
allocated on your rotor and wait there.

182
00:13:25,261 --> 00:13:30,260
If the tone becomes continuous,
that's when you evacuate your section.

183
00:13:30,359 --> 00:13:33,166
And you don't need
to ring 999, because the

184
00:13:33,190 --> 00:13:36,272
system contacts the
fire service automatically.

185
00:13:36,659 --> 00:13:39,260
Your job is people, not phone calls.

186
00:13:40,259 --> 00:13:41,260
One last thing.

187
00:13:42,109 --> 00:13:45,260
I'd really encourage you all to come
to the dress rehearsal on the 12th.

188
00:13:46,109 --> 00:13:50,260
Now, it isn't so that you can see the show
for nothing, although of course you will.

189
00:13:50,459 --> 00:13:53,260
And it's not really a chance
to meet the actors either.

190
00:13:53,409 --> 00:13:55,260
They're far too busy and nervous to chat.

191
00:13:56,059 --> 00:13:58,647
The point is that you'll
find out exactly when the

192
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:01,272
sudden blackouts and the
very loud effects happen.

193
00:14:01,273 --> 00:14:04,260
There's a gunshot in Act 2, for instance.

194
00:14:05,009 --> 00:14:07,260
If you know it's coming,
you won't be caught out.

195
00:14:07,261 --> 00:14:10,260
And you can reassure anyone
in your section who's startled.

196
00:14:10,261 --> 00:14:13,260
Right, that's the talking done.

197
00:14:13,261 --> 00:14:15,260
Let's go and find those waistcoats.

198
00:14:15,261 --> 00:14:19,260
And then I'll walk you round so
you can see it all for yourselves.

199
00:14:20,309 --> 00:14:22,260
That is the end of Part 2.

200
00:14:23,109 --> 00:14:27,260
You now have one minute to
check your answers to Part 2.

201
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:53,260
I'll be right back.

202
00:14:53,261 --> 00:14:54,260
I'll be right back.

203
00:14:54,261 --> 00:14:55,261
Thank you.

204
